Peal Ahamed Shanto, a Ph.D. student at Texas Tech University, expressed interest in joining the University of Delaware's Department of Environmental Economics after being unable to secure a position in prior application cycles. Dr. James Rising acknowledged Peal’s previous high-ranking application but informed him of ongoing funding challenges and the likelihood of not accepting new students. He offered to keep Peal’s information in consideration for future openings. In later correspondence, Peal sought updates and confirmation on his application status, leading to a recommendation from Dr. Rising to reapply for consideration. Ultimately, Dr. Rising informed Peal that funding for new students was not available and suggested applying through the UD Economics program for potentially better funding options. Despite the disappointing outcome, Peal maintained a positive outlook on future collaboration opportunities.
